From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] flow: REPAIR_TIMING_PATH_GROUP restricts repair_timing to one group
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

repair_timing takes -path_group (reg2reg, in2reg, reg2out, in2out), and
the flow's repair_timing_helper had no way to pass it. A parent macro
whose ports are its blocks' pins carries set_max_delay budgets on paths
that run from one block, through the parent, into another; no repair
inside the parent alone meets them, and TNS_END_PERCENT's 1 % of
endpoints is spent on them while the register-to-register paths, the
ones that set the macro's period, are not touched. On XiangShan's
XSTile parent macro the grt repair's every iteration chased one block
pin at -5.4 ns and moved the reg2reg period by 2 ps; restricted to
reg2reg, capped at 1,600 iterations (patch 0164), it took the period
from 3,768 to 2,826 ps.

Empty, the default, repairs every group as before.

Not upstreamed; retires at a bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

---
